    "question": "Arnold owns three cars. The first car averages 50 miles per gallon of gas. The second car averages 10 miles per gallon of gas. And the third car averages 15 miles per gallon of gas. He splits his 450-mile monthly driving mileage equally amongst his three cars.  If gas costs $2 per gallon, how much does he spend on gas each month?",
    "gold": "56",
    "answer": "He drives each vehicle 150 miles because 450 / 3 = <<450/3=150>>150\nThe first car will need 3 gallons of gas because 150 / 50 = <<150/50=3>>3\nThe second car will need 15 gallons of gas because 150 / 10 = <<150/10=15>>15\nThe third car will need 10 gallons of gas because 150 / 15 = <<150/15=10>>10\nHe will need 28 gallons in total because 3 + 15 + 10 = <<3+15+10=28>>28\nThis will cost him $56 because 28 x $2 = $<<28*2=56>>56\n#### 56"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Arnold spends on gas each month, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the monthly driving mileage for each car:**\n   Arnold drives a total of 450 miles per month and splits this equally among his three cars.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Monthly driving mileage per car} = \\frac{450 \\text{ miles}}{3} = 150 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the amount of gas used by each car:**\n   - For the first car, which averages 50 miles per gallon:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gas used by the first car} = \\frac{150 \\text{ miles}}{50 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = 3 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n   - For the second car, which averages 10 miles per gallon:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gas used by the second car} = \\frac{150 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = 15 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n   - For the third car, which averages 15 miles per gallon:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gas used by the third car} = \\frac{150 \\text{ miles}}{15 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = 10 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total amount of gas used per month:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total gas used} = 3 \\text{ gallons} + 15 \\text{ gallons} + 10 \\text{ gallons} = 28 \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total cost of the gas:**\n   Gas costs $2 per gallon.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = 28 \\text{ gallons} \\times 2 \\text{ dollars per gallon} = 56 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nThus, Arnold spends \\(\\boxed{56}\\) dollars on gas each month.",
